# Multivibe parity (Cursor)

Thin mirrors of Multivibe desk habits. Law SOT stays `$MULTIVIBE_ROOT/law/`.

## One boss

Per task: **Cursor** (this agent / subagents / Cloud Agent) **or** `multivibe_send` — never both.

## Wax (standing memory)

Multi-step work when Wax MCP is available:

1. Early: `recall` (or `session_open` + recall) with project slug when known
2. As you go: `remember` short durable facts (decisions, paths, gotchas) — not transcripts
3. End / rotate: `remember` spine; prefer `session_close` when a session was opened

Skip Wax on one-line Q&A.

## RESULT shape (after hops)

Close implement/review hops with: **PASS/FAIL**, what changed, **verify cmd → exit N**. Do not claim ship without verify.

## Lanes / isolation

Non-trivial edits → `.worktrees/lane-*` first when in a git repo (same idea as Multivibe ⌘N). Cloud Agents already isolate per run.

## Cloud vs Mac

- **Crack Lab / Oracle** — Cloud Agent env Mad Crack Lab OK for walk-away; code ships via git → Oracle.
- **Multibot** — develop in Cursor; runtime stays Mac mini.
- Cloud gets Multivibe **skills/rules** via env sync; local IDE also has Multivibe **MCP**.

## GUI

Multi Vibe GUI is **frozen**. Use shipped app only when you need the lane rail / Ship UI. Kernel = this repo’s law/skills/`mv-call`.
